          "text": "The quickstart matches exactly one route for this request: **`position-aware-capability-negative`** (request: \"async func(u64) -> map<string,u64> as an ordinary public WAsmC value\"). Its `required_additional_reads` is empty and it names no check commands, so I use only its evidence and stop there — no manifests, history or implementation scans.\n\n## Answer, decided position by position\n\n**Source position (ordinary synchronous function accepting u64):** Supported. The route's `supported_positions` list admits `u64` as an ordinary local, a parameter, a result, and a nested source payload. AGENTS.md's product contract confirms: ordinary source supports `u32`, `u64`, signed integers, documented control flow, Option/Result and admitted aggregate positions; `u64` preserves width and signedness. So yes — the pinned release compiles an ordinary synchronous function that accepts `u64`.\n\n**Async position:** Unsupported. \"Ordinary async source\" is not supported by the v0.0.21 compiler. This is an independent stop, not caused by the `u64` part.\n\n**Public-value position (ordinary `map<string,u64>`):** Unsupported. A Map is resident/local only and is not a direct public WIT value result. This is also an independent stop, separate from the async limitation.\n\n**Host position:** Unchanged by the above. Compile the smallest complete source, inspect every generated import, and compare module/name/kind/signature against an application-owned exact allowlist before instantiating. A declared import is an effect request only — it grants no filesystem, network, clock, randomness, process, credential or device authority. Pure programs require `imports=[]` and `{}`. Never expose raw handles, private lanes, Store identities, lifecycle helpers or transfer plans in application source.\n\n## Semantics-preserving alternatives (unsupported positions only; no source generated)\n\n- `u32` or `i64` **only** with application-owned bounds and signedness proof\n- An ordere