          "text": "Task complete via the `ordinary-source-positive` route — one exact match, used only that route.\n\n**Source** — `examples/agent-quickstart/pair.wasmc` (smallest complete supported source; no glue was missing):\n\n```wasmc\npackage local:logical_pair;\n\ninterface api {\n  run: func(value: s32, flag: bool) -> tuple<bool, bool> {\n    return tuple(value != 0, flag);\n  }\n}\n\nworld app { export api; }\n```\n\n**Compile, import inspection, execution** — via `node examples/agent-quickstart/run-pair.mjs` (compiles with the pinned public facade `current/wasmc.mjs`, inspects, then instantiates):\n\n```json\n{\"accepted\":true,\"source\":\"examples/agent-quickstart/pair.wasmc\",\"core_bytes\":49,\"core_sha256\":\"55f3c7e3d09b564b89b8268299a69569a33b856b46405cb4c4dd51634afec84e\",\"imports\":[],\"exports\":[{\"name\":\"run\",\"kind\":\"function\"}],\"call\":\"run(5, true)\",\"result\":[1,1]}\n```\n\n**Exact evidence**\n- Core module: 49 bytes, `core_sha256` = `55f3c7e3d09b564b89b8268299a69569a33b856b46405cb4c4dd51634afec84e`\n- Imports: `[]` — pure program, instantiated with `{}` (host-authority boundary satisfied: every import checked, allowlist empty)\n- Exports: `run` (function)\n- Call: `run(5, true)` → `[1, 1]`\n\n**Embedding note:** the `tuple<bool, bool>` is one semantic result; JavaScript observes two flattened Core lanes (`[1, 1]`), not an automatically lifted object."
